{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.047,
            0.419,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": "3. The hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle is 10. What are its other two sidelengths? [**Hint:** Find the area of the square composed of two such right triangles.]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.162,
            0.337,
            0.181
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "General Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.185,
            0.847,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": "The relation between the areas of a square and the square on its diagonal can be used to find a general relation between the hypotenuse and the other two sides of an isosceles right triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.348,
            0.247,
            0.685,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.509,
            0.845,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": "Let a be the length of the equal sides and c the length of the hypotenuse."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.34,
            0.533,
            0.66,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "Area of SQVU = 2 × Area of PQRS"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.419,
            0.556,
            0.531,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": "S 0 , c ^ { 2 } = 2 \\bar { a } ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.581,
            0.845,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "This formula can be used to find c when a is known, or to find a when c is known."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.629,
            0.845,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 1:** Find the hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle whose equal sides have length 12."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.672,
            0.562,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "We have $a = 1 2$ . Using the formula, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.395,
            0.7,
            0.6,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": "c = \\sqrt{2 \\times 12^{2}} = \\sqrt{288}",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.732,
            0.476,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": "We have $1 6 ^ { 2 } = 2 5 6$ , and $1 7 ^ { 2 } = 2 8 9$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.757,
            0.474,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\sqrt { 2 8 8 }$ lies between 16 and 17."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.782,
            0.846,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": "The length of the hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle, whose length of the equal sides is 12 units, is between 16 and 17 units."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.83,
            0.846,
            0.87
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Example 2: If the hypotenuse of an isosceles right triangle is ${ \\sqrt { 7 2 } } ,$ find its other two sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.873,
            0.573,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "We have $c = { \\sqrt { 7 2 } } .$ . Using the formula, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.462,
            0.896,
            0.537,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": "c ^ { 2 }   = 2 a ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.093,
            0.922,
            0.129,
            0.942
          ],
          "content": "40"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
